// FML-ADR-081 cache-only build of the pi4b-arm64 profile (FML-ADR-088).
//
// apt-get(8), apt 3.0.3 (the tools-tree lock's apt): "--list-cleanup: This
// option is on by default; use --no-list-cleanup to turn it off. When it is
// on, apt-get will automatically manage the contents of /var/lib/apt/lists to
// ensure that obsolete files are erased. ... Configuration Item:
// APT::Get::List-Cleanup."
//
// mkosi 25.3 gives the amd64 tools tree and this arm64 image one package
// cache (__init__.py, finalize_default_tools) and one lists directory in it
// (installer/apt.py, subdir() is "apt"). The image syncs second, with
// APT::Architectures=arm64, and with the default here apt erases the tools
// tree's amd64 lists as obsolete. The network-isolated build then cannot
// install the tools tree: "E: Unable to locate package base-files" (CI,
// 2026-10-09). Omit this line and that failure returns. The lists never reach
// the image: they live in the package cache, not under the image root.
APT::Get::List-Cleanup "false";
